:c.the CHATBOT service machine&colon. source, data deck, the VM/370
changes (already installed on the system)
:etable.
:figcap.Kit contents
:efig.
:h1.ESA/390 Deviations of the Virtual Machine
:p.The ESA/390 virtual machine is complete enough for Linux. Where it
deviates from the architecture, the deviation is recorded in the
project's register (documents 39 and 40). The ones a user may
notice&colon.
:ul.
:li.A format-1 channel program is converted to format 0 in place while
it runs (any length; at most 32 TIC targets).
:li.No SCLP and no z/VM interfaces (DIAGNOSE codes of z/VM); Linux must
be told :xph.conmode=3215 condev=0x0009:exph..
:li.One processor; SIGP is answered for that processor only.
:li.Selector channels of an ESA/390 guest behave as block multiplexer
channels.
:li.Linux's machine-check handling is not exercised&colon. CP presents
no machine checks to the guest.
:eul.
:h1.CP and CMS Command Tables
:p.These tables are generated from the system itself
(:xph.tools/cmdtables.py:exph., document 50 in the repository)&colon.
the CP commands from CP's command table in DMKCFC, in the order CP
searches it; the QUERY and SET operands from its operand lists; the CMS
commands from the nucleus function table and from the MODULE and EXEC
files on the system disks. :hp2.Abbrev:ehp2. is the shortest form CP
accepts, :hp2.Class:ehp2. the privilege class (any&colon. no class
needed). :hp2.+:ehp2. marks a VM/370plus addition or change.
:h2.CP commands
:p.From the :xph.COMND:exph. table in DMKCFC (CE source plus XA0054DK,
XA0055DK), in table order (CP searches it in this order, so an
abbreviation goes to the first match). :hp1.Abbrev:ehp1. is the shortest
accepted form; :hp1.Class:ehp1. is the privilege class (any = no class
needed, also before LOGON).
:fig.
:table cols='1500 1100 1000 1500 4538'.
